est) · out of scope · handoff.\n29\t\n30\t## Budgets\n31\t\n32\tTarget ≤ ~600 tokens per contract; hard ceiling **1500 estimated tokens** (`ceil(chars/4)`) —\n33\tsized to the largest legitimate exemplar (Q0). Over the ceiling = split the contract.\n34\t\n35\t## State lives on the board, never in the file\n36\t\n37\tContracts are immutable once signed (amendments are logged authoring defects, Q0 precedent).\n38\t`todo/claimed/verify/done/blocked` is derived from `delivery/board/BOARD.md` + `LOG.md` today and\n39\tfrom the B-ledger after B2. The validator asserts every task id appears **exactly once** across\n40\tboard columns (AUTHORED = deps not yet DONE) and exactly once in `TRACEABILITY.md`.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope enters through the plan\n43\t\n44\t`plan-deps.json` mirrors plan §12 (+hotfix ids) and is updated only with a plan rev. A task file\n45\twithout a plan phase, or a phase without a task file, fails the gate — nothing is lost, nothing is\n46\tinvented. The dependency graph must be acyclic.\n47\t"}]},"uuid":"8fc55df5-981d-4bdf-8a9b-fbb20a2e8971","timestamp":"2026-07-25T13:58:46.752Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\architecture\\SPEC-work-contracts.md","content":"# SPEC — Work contracts (W0)\n\n> A work item is to human/agent work what a pypes manifest is to data work: a declarative,\n> versioned contract executed by small composable services (selector W1, sandbox W2, verifier).\n> Validator: `server/coordination/work-schema/validate.mjs` · Gate: `node scripts/gates/w0.mjs`\n> Canonical backlog: `delivery/tasks/` (one markdown file per item; `backlog/` naming is superseded).\n\n## Format (one file, `delivery/tasks/<ID>.md`)\n\nYAML frontmatter — all fields required unless noted:\n\n| field | rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| `id` | equals the filename; `[A-Z]\\d+` or `M2-\\d+` |\n| `epic` | an existing `delivery/epics/EP-*.md` |\n| `milestone` | `M1` or `M2` |\n| `okr` | non-empty; the id must sit in