{"parentUuid":"b9e26260-db10-4b23-8d0f-bf6249ff7e61","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"11e05ef6-b4ac-48ab-a0e6-210bd228eed8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016hMWhcufEiQYgKviLpspSa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: house-trainer\n3\tdescription: Operate the EP-T house-method QLoRA trainer end-to-end on the T480 eGPU — dataset builds (T2), training/eval/GGUF (T3+), verification, and the data-quality levers. Use when training, evaluating, rebuilding the dataset, verifying a T-task, or extending Workstream T.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# house-trainer — the EP-T QLoRA pipeline playbook\n7\t\n8\tEverything here was proven live on the trainer (T0–T3, LOG 2026-07-22..24). Follow it and\n9\tyou skip a week of Windows-ROCm debugging. **Read the two absolutes first.**\n10\t\n11\t## Absolutes\n12\t\n13\t1. **Privacy:** job-application/CV content NEVER enters training data. Every build runs\n14\t   the leak gate (`scripts/train/lib/privacy.mjs` → `scripts/longview/lib/leak_gate.mjs`).\n15\t   Quarantined sids (live home + sessions workspace `quarantine.json`) are dropped\n16\t   structurally. Generated rows are git-ignored — never commit them. Never weaken\n17\t   `scripts/train/dataset/personal_terms.json` to make a build pass.\n18\t2. **Honesty:** rubric (`scripts/train/eval/rubric.md`) is frozen BEFORE training. If a\n19\t   run invalidates an earlier number, the correction goes on the record\n20\t   (docs/train/T3-eval-report.md v1→v2 precedent). Tuned-worse is a valid, logged result.\n21\t\n22\t## Liveness — NEVER trust a tqdm log for a long GPU job\n23\t\n24\tThe eGPU **wedges transiently** (TB3/RDNA4): a step hangs, the process stays alive but blocked,\n25\tworking set collapses to ~MB, and the tqdm log freezes looking exactly like \"slow\". A DPO run\n26\tsat wedged at step 8/38 for 6 h this way. **Prove liveness, don't infer it:**\n27\t- log mtime vs now (`stat -c %y <log>`) — hours stale on a minutes-long job = wedged;\n28\t- two CPU-time snapshots ~90 s apart (`Get-CimInstance Win32_Process ... UserModeTime+KernelModeTime`)\n29\t  — a live job burns CPU seconds, a wedged one doesn't;\n30\t- advancing artifacts (trainer/checkpoint-*, *_result.json, adapter files).\n31\tRecover: `Stop-Process -Id <pid> -Force` (PowerShell; use `$procId`, `$id:` is a parse error) →\n32\tdevice-matmul health check → relaunch with a lower `max_length` (memory pressure wedges gfx1200).\n33\t\n34\t## Environment (measured, don't rediscover)\n35\t\n36\t- GPU: RX 9060 XT **gfx1200**, 15.92 GiB, Razer Core X TB3, native-Windows ROCm.\n37\t- Trainer venv python: `C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.unsloth\\studio\\unsloth_studio\\Scripts\\python.exe`\n38\t  (torch 2.11.0+rocm7.13.0 / hip 7.13.99004 / Unsloth 2026.7.4 / bnb rocm714).\n39\t- **Training requires a vcvars64 shell** (Triton JIT): write a CRLF .bat that `call`s\n40\t  `C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual Studio\\2022\\BuildTools\\VC\\Auxiliary\\Build\\vcvars64.bat`\n41\t  then runs the venv python; launch from Git Bash as `cmd.exe //c '<single-quoted-path>'`\n42\t  (double slash beats MSYS path-mangling; never pipe the launch through `head`).\n43\t  Eager eval (`run_eval.py`) needs no vcvars.\n44\t- llama.cpp ROCm build: `~\\.unsloth\\llama.cpp\\build\\bin\\Release\\` (`llama-server.exe`,\n45\t  `llama-quantize.exe`); bundled `gguf-py` for structural reads. node: `~\\.unsloth\\node`.\n46\t- **Parallelism 1**: one GPU job at a time, batch 1 (+grad accum), workers 0.\n47\t- **Disk:** stage fp16 downloads + merges on D: (`HF_HOME=D:\\t3-merge\\hf`,\n48\t  `T3_GGUF_DIR=D:\\t3-merge\\gguf`) — ~30 GB peak for a 7B; C: cannot take it.\n49\t- Corpus: home clone `D:\\benny-home` (PRIME_SILO_HOME), memo-ray `~\\.mem0ray\\data`\n50\t  (80,555 entities), big LONGVIEW workspace\n51\t  `D:\\benny-home\\benny\\workspaces\\sessions_v1` (376 JSON cards + data_out prose).\n52\t\n53\t## Pipeline (each step gated)\n54\t\n55\t```bash\n56\t# 1. Dataset (T2) — build + validate (leak gate, schema, disjoint split)\n57\tT2_TRACE_MAX_ENTITIES=80555 T2_TRACE_MAX_ROWS=5000 node scripts/gates/t2.mjs\n58\tnode --test scripts/train/tests/build_dataset_test.mjs scripts/train/tests/build_dataset_v3_test.mjs\n59\t\n60\t# 2. Gold sample for owner hand-audit (deterministic, stratified)\n61\tnode scripts/train/audit_sample.mjs --n 200\n62\t\n63\t# 3. Baseline eval FIRST (proves the instrument; re-run whenever the split changes)\n64\t<venv-python> scripts/train/eval/run_eval.py --mode base --out scripts/train/eval/out/base.json\n65\t\n66\t# 4. Train (vcvars .bat wrapper; ~100 min for ~2.3k examples x 2 epochs)\n67\tT3_EPOCHS=2 T3_A_OVERSAMPLE=2 <venv-python> scripts/train/qlora/train_qlora.py\n68\t\n69\t# 5. Tuned eval (same split, same instrument)\n70\t<venv-python> scripts/train/eval/run_eval.py --mode tuned --adapter scripts/train/qlora/out/adapter --out scripts/train/eval/out/tuned.json\n71\t\n72\t# 6. Merge -> GGUF (STAGE ON D:) + gate\n73\tHF_HOME=D:\\t3-merge\\hf T3_GGUF_DIR=D:\\t3-merge\\gguf <venv-python> scripts/train/qlora/merge_gguf.py\n74\tpython scripts/gates/t3.py   # GREEN iff tuned.agg_nll <= base.agg_nll AND GGUF loads\n75\t```\n76\t\n77\tTimings: NLL-only eval (`--no-gen-match`) ~15 min; full eval with greedy tool-match ~1 h;\n78\ttrain ~100 min; merge ~1–1.5 h (dominated by fp16 download if not cached).\n79\t\n80\t## Architecture invariants (why it looks the way it does)\n81\t\n82\t- `scripts/train/qlora/format.py` is the ONE formatting module — training labels and eval\n83\t  NLL both come from `encode_nll` (prompt masked with -100). Never let them diverge, or\n84\t  the base-vs-tuned delta measures prompt drift, not learning.\n85\t- Training uses **plain HF Trainer over pre-tokenized rows**, NOT Unsloth's SFTTrainer\n86\t  dataset path — its multiprocess tokenize-map dies on Windows (spawn/dill can't import\n87\t  the generated UnslothSFTTrainer; `dataset_num_proc=1` doesn't help).\n88\t- Eager paths import `torchao_stub.py` before transformers (no Windows-ROCm torchao).\n89\t- Unsloth writes GGUFs to `<requested-dir>_gguf` — glob both.\n90\t- RAG stays DISABLED in eval — the number must be the fine-tune's own contribution\n91\t  (method in weights, facts in RAG; no KG fact-recall rows, no synthetic paraphrases).\n92\t\n93\t## Data levers & current state\n94\t\n95\t`docs/train/DATA-PLAN-v3.md` is the live plan; `docs/train/T2-dataset-card.md` has the\n96\tv1→v2 defect history (the 63%-empty-args lesson: **audit targets, not just schemas** —\n97\tmedian target length and duplicate-rate are the tells). Stream A sources are in\n98\t`scripts/train/lib/{corpus_v3,streams_v3}.mjs`; add a new source = new reader + pair\n99\tbuilder + red-first test + schema source.type + leak-gate wiring in build_dataset.mjs.\n100\tRollups/KG = RAG material, never training rows.\n101\t\n102\t## T4 — serving behind the router (LM Studio + eGPU)\n103\t\n104\tAdditive candidate: `runtime/benny/router/tuned_engine.py` registers `house/…` in MODEL_REGISTRY\n105\t+ wraps `resolve_executor` (default engine unchanged, reversible). Serve the GGUF via LM Studio\n106\ton the eGPU (copy into `~/.lmstudio/models/<pub>/<repo>-GGUF/`, `lms load <modelKey> --gpu max\n107\t--identifier <id>`; `lms import` hangs headless). Gate `scripts/gates/t4.py` = structural\n108\t(litellm-free) + live offload through the ADR-004 `run_task`. Gotchas: LM Studio 400s\n109\t`response_format:json_object` (fixed provider-agnostically in `offload/gate.py::run_judge`); use a\n110\tFAST non-reasoning judge (gemma-3-4b), different family from the executor (anti-collusion); never\n111\trun the live gate during a training run. See [[lmstudio-egpu-serving]].\n112\t\n113\t## T5 — DPO (preference tuning)\n114\t\n115\tSelf-generated hard negatives: `scripts/train/dpo/build_prefs.py` asks the SERVED SFT model\n116\t(LM Studio) for greedy answers on TRAIN-split prompts; where wrong vs the corpus reference, emit\n117\t`(chosen=reference, rejected=SFT-answer)`. **Filter to method signal** — keep tool-selection\n118\terrors + voice-drift; DROP arg-value mismatches (that's memorising RAG facts, against the doctrine).\n119\t`train_dpo.py`: `PatchDPOTrainer()` first, load the SFT adapter as policy, `ref_model=None`,\n120\tbeta 0.1, lr 5e-6 (≪ SFT's 2e-4), 1 epoch, max_length ≤1024. SFT baseline eval = reuse the last\n121\tSFT tuned.json (same adapter+split, deterministic). Gate `scripts/gates/t5.py`: GREEN iff\n122\t`dpo.agg_nll ≤ sft.agg_nll` + merged GGUF loads. DPO-not-beating-SFT is a valid logged result.\n123\t\n124\t## Verification protocol (author≠verifier)\n125\t\n126\tLog as `claude-tN-verifier`. Reproduce, don't trust: re-run the NLL instrument fresh\n127\t(deterministic — must match to ~6 decimals), own split-overlap check, NEGATIVE tests\n128\t(swap base/tuned reports → expect RED tuned_worse; empty GGUF dir → RED gguf_missing;\n129\tseeded CV row → t2 RED), own llama-server /health smoke, then gate re-run. Move\n130\tVERIFY→DONE on the board + LOG with caveats stated (same-session verify is a named\n131\tcaveat, precedent T2/T3).\n132\t\n133\t## Current board state (2026-07-25)\n134\t\n135\tT0/T1/T2/T3 DONE+verified. **T3 v3** (data-plan-v3, all pre-registered criteria passed):\n136\ttuned Qwen2.5-Coder-7B **−57% agg NLL vs base** (2.6195→1.1253, A −38.3%, RAG off);\n137\tGGUF `D:\\t3-merge\\gguf_gguf\\…Q4_K_M.gguf`, also in LM Studio as `qwen2.5-coder-tuned`.\n138\t**T4 DONE (in VERIFY)** — tuned wired behind the router, live ADR-004 offload passed, judge 1.0.\n139\t**T5 (DPO) in progress** — 303 method pairs, first run wedged (relaunched, max_len 1024).\n140\tOwner still owes the 200-row gold hand-audit (human-signed). KR1.5 closes on T5 verify.\n141\t"}]},"uuid":"d7f36376-af0c-4295-8ffa-e88758b14c01","timestamp":"2026-07-25T13:58:53.863Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\.claude\\skills\\house-trainer\\SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: house-trainer\ndes