{"parentUuid":"1095bc85-9404-4e88-acfe-17ed46ada8bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdNuGM11LJe8juJwjndVx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The design is authored. Here's what landed in [SOLUTION-longview-self-learning.md](prime-silo/architecture/SOLUTION-longview-self-learning.md) (§4–§6, Status flipped to DRAFT):\n\n## The organizing idea (§4.0)\nThe repo already runs three append-only, chain-hashed, `fold(events)→state`, non-blocking logs — B0 `coordination/tasks.jsonl`, G0 `runs/<id>/events.jsonl`, and the delivery `LOG.md`. Rather than invent a new persistence model, the flywheel **adds one more log of the same shape**: the **knowledge event log (KEL)** on D:. Everything else is that log, a **projection** off it, or a **guard** around it. That's the \"reuse §2, don't rebuild\" discipline made literal.\n\n## Architecture (§4) — how the 11 steers compose\n- **KEL = truth** (steer 1): Neo4j/Chroma/memo-ray/cards are rebuildable projections; envelope carries valid-time + txn-time (R1), HLC (steer 7), `time_confidence` (steer 8), authorship (R38), `schema_version` + converters (steer 10), `prev` chain-hash. Corrections are new events, never mutations.\n- **Staging on D:** full hybrid — CAS blobs (de-dup) + human-navigable index + self-describing manifest (steer 2), with the **R40 inbound poison gate** as the mirror of the outbound leak gate, and **R41 durability** (replicate + checksum + restore drill).\n- **Delta**: per-content-hash cursors (steer 3); HLC valid-time makes it ordering-tolerant.\n- **Execution register**: one SQLite projection folding the four existing logs, backfilled (steer 4).\n- **Loop**: `flywheel-daemon`, file-watch + cron, each turn gated by a **B0 `wx` single-winner lease** — R43 exactly-once reusing B0 unchanged, no new mutual-exclusion mechanism.\n- **Safety guards** where self-learning actually risks it: full-hybrid liveness (steer 11, encodes the [[verify-gpu-job-liveness]] lesson), R38 collapse guard (verifier gate + house-fraction cap), R39 human-signed promotion + rollback with an explicit R44 decision function.\n- **§4.8 maps every one of R1–R45 to a component.**\n\n## Schema/DDL (§5)\nConcrete shapes: KEL event envelope, CAS/index/manifest layout, delta cursor, the `execution_register.sqlite` DDL (with the R16 cross-machine comparison index), and the signed served-model/promotion record.\n\n## Task breakdown (§6)\nNew epic **EP-L**, tasks **L0–L14** across the three waves in W0 contract format — acyclic dependency graph, wave-1 spine `L0→L1→{L2,L3,L4}→L5→L6` + L7 (the R17 \"stage to D: now\" quick win plus its guards). **L0 and L2 are drafted as full board-ready contracts inline** to seed authoring. Milestone M4 — I flagged that the `w0` validator's milestone enum needs an additive bump, which is itself a nice steer-10-consistent change.\n\nTwo things I decided rather than asked, both flagged in-doc: epic letter **EP-L** (A–G/Q/R/T/W are taken) and milestone **M4**. I did **not** commit — the edit sits in the working tree for your review, consistent with the human-signed-stops doctrine. When you're ready, the next move is authoring the wave-1 `L*.md` contracts + `EP-L.md` + traceability wiring, and staging this session as tagged training material per §8's dogfood mandate."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":114895,"output_tokens":1272,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1272,"cache_read_input_tokens":114895,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId"