n memory, and transactional guarantees aren't critical here.\n\nSo the recommendation is clear: make JSONL the default projection in the spec, keep it human-readable and file-based, and relegate SQLite or DuckDB to an optional optimization you measure first. I should offer to update the document directly since this is exactly the kind of design amendment that surfaces during review. I'll keep my response concise and avoid unnecessary elaboration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31,"cache_read_input_tokens":118788,"output_tokens":3570,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3570,"cache_read_input_tokens":118788,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdNxnxGVcoFESFXTpm6zg","type":"assistant","uuid":"52bd30e1-8fac-4f05-8152-de0b8803bc4b","timestamp":"2026-07-25T14:51:25.805Z","effort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"468ee845-7d82-4724-a78a-d2a9fbbb431e","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"52bd30e1-8fac-4f05-8152-de0b8803bc4b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdNxnynmcaKQa3RsZaSUd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your instinct is right. Let me be honest about what SQLite actually buys here versus what it costs.\n\n**The key fact: the execution register is already a *projection*, not truth.** Truth is the four source logs (G0 events, train JSONs, LONGVIEW ledger, B0 ledger). So the register is a rebuildable cache. The only question is what format that cache takes — and SQLite's real strengths don't apply:\n\n- **ACID / transactions** — not needed; it's a single-writer rebuild from logs, never a live transactional store.\n- **Concurrent multi-reader** — the dashboard is one process. Not needed.\n- **Joins / foreign keys** — `lineage_edge ↔ execution` folds in memory trivially at this scale.\n\nWhat's actually left as a benefit is **indexed analytical queries for R16** (\"model A on machine X vs model B on machine Y — cost/quality delta\") without a full scan. That only bites at scale.\n\n**What it costs is real and cuts against the design's spine:**\n- It introduces the repo's **first database**. Everything else — coordination/, runs/, cards, the whole thing — is deliberately file-based JSONL. §4 opens with \"reuse, don't rebuild\"; adding a DB is the opposite.\n- **Two schema-evolution stories**: the JSONL converter registry (steer 10) *and* SQLite `ALTER TABLE`. That's the complexity you're smelling.\n- Binary file on D: — doesn't diff, isn't human-readable, and is less recoverable than newline-JSON if the drive corrupts a page (R41 territory).\n\n**Recommendation — downgrade SQLite to an additive, measure-first fallback.** Default the register to `executions.jsonl`, folded exactly like every other log: one doctrine, human-readable, one schema story, zero new tech. If R16 query latency at real corpus scale ever proves the fold too slow, materialize an index *then