e unchanged.\n4. Converter test: an event at schema_version 1.0.0 with a 1.0.0→1.1.0 up-converter replays without error.\n\n## Acceptance (BDD — every Scenario must map to an automated test)\n```gherkin\nFeature: the knowledge event log is truth; stores are projections\n  Scenario: a correction never mutates history\n    Given a card_asserted event E1 at txn_time T1\n    When a card_asserted event E2 supersedes E1 at txn_time T2\n    Then folding at txn_time T1 still yields E1, folding now yields E2, and E1's raw line is unchanged\n  Scenario: the chain betrays an edited historical line\n    Given a KEL with N appended events\n    When any historical line is edited\n    Then the validator reports the 1-based line number whose prev-hash no longer matches\n  Scenario: bi-temporal queries are answerable\n    Given events with distinct valid_time and txn_time\n    When folded with a valid_time<=T predicate and separately a txn_time<=T predicate\n    Then each returns the correct historical state for that axis\n  Scenario: an out-of-version record still replays\n    Given an event at schema_version 1.0.0 and a converter 1.0.0->1.1.0\n    When the projector folds the log\n    Then the event is up-converted and projected without error\n  Scenario: a write failure never raises\n    Given a KEL file that cannot be written\n    When an append is attempted\n    Then it degrades to a logged no-op and the caller is unaffected\n```\n\n## Out of scope\nThe staging store (L1), the actual projectors/time-travel query (L8), the execution register (L5).\nEnvelope + fold + converter mechanics only. The milestone-enum bump is already done (authoring-time).\n\n## Handoff\nVerifier re-runs `node scripts/gates/l0.mjs` from a clean checkout with a fixture log.\n`architecture/SPEC-knowledge-eventlog.md` committed as the normative envelope spec.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_to