{"parentUuid":"b2d9d57b-adab-4675-93b3-96157c1de416","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdP1h1Ly79GJztdCM5iQS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015hJ2Cx9bCtRBHskte5GdPU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\delivery\\tasks\\L8.md","content":"---\nid: L8\nepic: EP-L\nmilestone: M5\nokr: O2.KR2.2\ndeps: [L0, L4]\nauthority: agent-ok\nallowlist: [server/coordination/lib/projector.mjs, server/coordination/lib/timetravel.mjs, tests/projector/, scripts/gates/l8.mjs]\ntools: [node]\nsandbox: worktree\nverify: node scripts/gates/l8.mjs\nbudget: 600\n---\n\n# L8 — Bi-temporal projectors + time-travel query\n\n## Goal\nFold the knowledge event log to rebuild the stores as projections, applying the L0 up-converter\nregistry, and answer both \"what was true at T\" (valid-time) and \"what did we know at T\"\n(transaction-time) — including reconstructing the exact knowledge state that produced an artifact\n(e.g. the corpus a model trained on). Projection is incremental via L4 cursors; rebuild-from-log is\nthe replay guarantee. R1–R3, R7, R32.\n\n## Context pointers (never inline content)\n- Design: architecture/SOLUTION-longview-self-learning.md §4.1 (projection) + §5.1/§5.6 (envelope, converters); steers 1/10\n- Inputs: L0 kel.mjs (fold + converters), L4 delta.mjs (incremental cursors)\n- Card projection (JSON on disk) is the reference sink proving the engine; Neo4j/Chroma/memo-ray adapters\n  conform to the same projection-sink interface (thin, additive — never replace the live write path, R36)\n- Requirements R1–R3, R7, R32\n\n## TDD plan\n1. Rebuild test red: folding a fixture KEL reproduces the card projection; delete + re-fold is identical.\n2. Valid-time test: query at valid_time T returns the world-state true at T, ignoring later corrections.\n3. Txn-time test: query at txn_time T returns what the system had recorded by T (knowledge-as-of).\n4. Corpus-reconstruction test: given a model's knowledge_watermark, the exact input state is rebuilt.\n5. Incremental test: a single changed session reprojects only affected records (via L4 cursors), not all.\n\n## Acceptance (BDD — every Scenario must map to an automated test)\n```gherkin\nFeature: projections are rebuildable and time-travellable off the log\n  Scenario: a projection rebuilds from the log alone\n    Given a KEL fixture and its card projection\n    When the projection is deleted and re-folded\n    Then the result is identical (rebuildable = replay)\n  Scenario: what was true at T (valid-time)\n    Given events later corrected\n    When the projection is queried at valid_time T\n    Then it returns the state true in the world at T, not the later correction\n  Scenario: what did we know at T (transaction-time)\n    Given events recorded across several transaction times\n    When the projection is queried at txn_time T\n    Then it returns only what had been recorded by T\n  Scenario: reconstruct the corpus a model trained on\n    Given an execution record with a knowledge_watermark\n    When the state is rebuilt at that watermark\n    Then it equals the exact input knowledge state of that training run\n  Scenario: a change reprojects incrementally\n    Given one changed session\n    When projection runs\n    Then only the affected records are rebuilt, not the whole store\n```\n\n## Out of scope\nPrivacy/quarantine filtering and conflict handling (L9). The loop that triggers projection (L10).\nReal Neo4j/Chroma/memo-ray service wiring is smoke-only here — cards are the deterministic reference sink.\n\n## Handoff\nVerifier re-runs `node scripts/gates/l8.mjs` from a clean checkout against the KEL fixture, confirming\nthe delete-and-rebuild identity, both time axes, corpus reconstruction, and incremental reprojection.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_