{"parentUuid":"1276f606-f15b-4830-ae58-d769be49c84c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdP1iWKGtotQG19Xtc6P2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012wUZ9UzJvqZ1cFtZWkWs3a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\delivery\\tasks\\L9.md","content":"---\nid: L9\nepic: EP-L\nmilestone: M5\nokr: O1.KR1.5\ndeps: [L8]\nauthority: human-signed\nallowlist: [server/coordination/lib/projector.mjs, server/coordination/lib/privacy_history.mjs, tests/privacy_history/, scripts/gates/l9.mjs]\ntools: [node]\nsandbox: worktree\nverify: node scripts/gates/l9.mjs\nbudget: 450\n---\n\n# L9 — Privacy-honoring history + keep-both-and-flag conflict\n\n## Goal\nAt projection, the leak-gate + quarantine/teleport filter applies so teleported sids never enter any\nprojection at any point in bi-temporal time; privacy deletions are tombstone events (moved, journalled,\nreversible — never hard-erased); and semantic conflicts are kept-both-and-flagged — two events\ncontradicting at the same valid-time are BOTH projected with a conflict marker plus a conflict_flagged\nreview event, never auto-picked. R4, R6, R31; steer 9.\n\n## Context pointers (never inline content)\n- Design: architecture/SOLUTION-longview-self-learning.md §4.1 (conflict/privacy at projection) + §4.7; steer 9\n- Reuse (reference, do not modify): scripts/longview/lib/leak_gate.mjs, longview/quarantine.json (teleported sids)\n- Hooks into L8's projector.mjs; tombstone semantics extend the teleport \"moves, never deletes\" doctrine\n- Requirements R4, R6, R31\n\n## TDD plan\n1. Time-travel exclusion test red: a teleported sid is absent from projections at every valid/txn time.\n2. Tombstone test: a privacy deletion tombstones + quarantines the record (reversible), never hard-erases.\n3. Conflict test: two contradictory events at the same valid_time both project with a conflict marker\n   and emit a conflict_flagged review event; neither is auto-selected.\n\n## Acceptance (BDD — every Scenario must map to an automated test)\n```gherkin\nFeature: history honors privacy and never silently picks a winner\n  Scenario: a teleported sid stays excluded across all time\n    Given a sid teleported to quarantine\n    When projections are queried at any valid-time or transaction-time\n    Then the sid's records never appear\n  Scenario: a privacy deletion is reversible, not erased\n    Given a record requiring privacy deletion\n    When it is removed\n    Then it is tombstoned and quarantined (journalled, restorable), not hard-erased\n  Scenario: contradictory facts are kept and flagged\n    Given two events asserting contradictory facts at the same valid_time\n    When the projection is built\n    Then both are present with a conflict marker and a conflict_flagged review event is emitted\n    And neither is auto-selected as the winner\n```\n\n## Out of scope\nThe verifier/human UI that resolves flagged conflicts (surfaced, not resolved here). Outbound\ndeliverable leak scanning (unchanged). Projection engine mechanics (L8).\n\n## Handoff\nVerifier re-runs `node scripts/gates/l9.mjs`, confirming the teleport-exclusion holds across both time\naxes, the tombstone is reversible, and the keep-both-and-flag NEGATIVE case (an auto-picked winner)\ngoes RED. Honors the same quarantine.json the T2 dataset build and LONGVIEW inventory already read.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1469,"cache_read_input_tokens":185488,"output_tokens":1266,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1469,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1266,"cache_read_input_tokens":185488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1469,"cache_creat