{"parentUuid":"3c39872e-016e-4a7c-b9d3-d58f72164be5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\delivery\\tasks\\L14.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\delivery\\tasks\\L14.md","content":"---\nid: L14\nepic: EP-L\nmilestone: M6\nokr: O2.KR2.2\ndeps: [L5, L10]\nauthority: agent-ok\nallowlist: [server/coordination/lib/triad_dashboard.mjs, server/pages/flywheel.html, tests/triad_dashboard/, scripts/gates/l14.mjs]\ntools: [node]\nsandbox: worktree\nverify: node scripts/gates/l14.mjs\nbudget: 500\n---\n\n# L14 — Compound-value triad dashboard\n\n## Goal\nProve the flywheel turns: a dashboard view showing the triad together — held-out eval delta (the honest\nanchor) + agent task pass-rate + cost/task — over loop turns, never collapsed into one gameable\ncomposite. Compound value measured end-to-end (sessions↑ → coverage↑ → eval↑ → agent success↑ / cost↓),\nnot just per-component metrics. R23, R24, R26, R30; steer 6.\n\n## Context pointers (never inline content)\n- Design: architecture/SOLUTION-longview-self-learning.md §4.5 (triad) + §4.6; steer 6 (triad, not composite)\n- Data source: L5 executions.jsonl (folds eval quality, agent pass-rate, cost per turn); reuse the existing ledger-sourced dashboard style\n- Optimization targets are explicit + versioned (R30); a non-improving turn is shown honestly, not hidden (R24)\n- Requirements R23, R24, R26, R30\n\n## TDD plan\n1. Triad test red: the view renders three separate series (eval delta, pass-rate, cost/task) per turn — no single composite.\n2. Honest-negative test: a non-improving turn is displayed (flagged), not omitted.\n3. Provenance test: each point traces to the executions.jsonl records it summarizes (auditable).\n4. Determinism test: the view is a pure function of the register (same input → same render).\n\n## Acceptance (BDD — every Scenario must map to an automated test)\n```gherkin\nFeature: the flywheel's compound value is visible and honest\n  Scenario: the triad is shown together, not composited\n    Given executions across several loop turns\n    When the dashboard renders\n    Then eval delta, agent pass-rate, and cost/task appear as three series over turns, with no single composite score\n  Scenario: a non-improving turn is not hidden\n    Given a turn whose eval regressed\n    When the dashboard renders\n    Then the turn is shown and flagged, not omitted\n  Scenario: each point is auditable\n    Given a rendered data point\n    When it is drilled\n    Then it traces to the executions.jsonl records it summarizes\n```\n\n## Out of scope\nThe decision rule (L13) and promotion (L12) — the dashboard shows, it does not decide or promote.\nNew metric collection (comes from L5). Presentation + honesty only.\n\n## Handoff\nVerifier re-runs `node scripts/gates/l14.mjs` from a clean checkout against a register fixture,\nconfirming three distinct series (no composite), the honest-negative turn is shown, and the render is\na deterministic function of executions.jsonl. Closes EP-L wave 3.\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}},"displayPath":"prime-silo\\delivery\\tasks\\L14.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3d270da4-a911-4651-9dbc-d73312b22caa","timestamp":"2026-07-25T20:37:59.242Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"468ee845-7d82-4724-a78a-d2a9fbbb431e","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"logical-weaving-pancake"}
{"parentUuid":"3d270da4-a911-4651-9dbc-d73312b22caa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\delivery\\tasks\\L13.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\delivery\\tasks\\L13.md","content":"---\nid: L13\nepic: EP-L\nmilestone: M6\nokr: O1.KR1.5\ndeps: [L12]\nauthority: human-signed\nallowlist: [server/coordination/lib/promotion_rule.mjs, scripts/train/eval/slices/, tests/promotion_rule/, scripts/gates/l13.mjs]\ntools: [node]\nsandbox: worktree\nverify: node scripts/gates/l13.mjs\nbudget: 400\n---\n\n# L13 — Promotion decision function + additive eval growth\n\n## Goal\n\"N+1 ≥ N\" is an explicit dominance/decision rule over the metric vector (eval NLL, agent pass-rate,\ncost, latency), specifying the outcome when metrics trade off (Pareto case) so \"better\" is decided by\nrule, not relitigated per turn. And the held-out instrument grows additively — new slices added without\ninvalidating the historical cross-turn series. Extends R23/R30/R37 and R24. R44, R45.\n\n## Context pointers (never inline content)\n- Design: architecture/SOLUTION-longview-self-learning.md §4.6 (R44/R45) + §5.5 (decision_vector, slice added_in_turn)\n- Metric vector comes from L5 executions.jsonl (eval_nll, agent_pass, cost, latency); eval anchor is the honest one\n- Slice tagging: each held-out slice carries added_in_turn; cross-turn comparison uses only slices present in both turns\n- Requirements R44, R45\n\n## TDD plan\n1. Dominance test red: a candidate better on all metrics returns \"promote\"; worse on all returns \"reject\".\n2. Pareto test: a candidate trading eval-gain for cost-loss resolves by the stated rule (eval-anchored), deterministically.\n3. Additive-eval test: adding a new slice with a later added_in_turn does not change any historical turn's series.\n4. Comparability test: two turns are compared only on slices present in both (new slices extend, never invalidate).\n\n## Acceptance (BDD — every Scenario must map to an automated test)\n```gherkin\nFeature: \"better\" is a rule, and the eval set grows without breaking history\n  Scenario: strict dominance decides\n    Given a candidate better on every metric\n    When the decision rule runs\n    Then it returns promote; and a candidate worse on every metric returns reject\n  Scenario: a Pareto trade-off resolves by rule\n    Given a candidate that gains eval but loses on cost\n    When the decision rule runs\n    Then it resolves deterministically by the stated eval-anchored rule, not per-turn relitigation\n  Scenario: a new eval slice does not rewrite history\n    Given a new held-out slice tagged with the current turn\n    When the cross-turn series is recomputed\n    Then earlier turns' scores are unchanged and comparisons use only slices shared by both turns\n```\n\n## Out of scope\nThe human-signed swap + rollback mechanism (L12 — this task only decides the verdict the human then\nsigns). Generating eval content (EP-T). The dashboard rendering (L14).\n\n## Handoff\nVerifier re-runs `node scripts/gates/l13.mjs`, confirming the Pareto case is deterministic and the\nadditive-slice scenario leaves historical turns byte-identical (frozen-for-honesty preserved).\n","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}},"displayPath":"prime-silo\\delivery\\tasks\\L13.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8c2c115f-3cfe-4080-8971-0565b461750c","timestamp":"2026-07-25T20:37:59.242Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"468ee845-7d82-4724-a78a-d2a9fbbb431e","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"logical-weaving-pancake"}
