{"parentUuid":"847621be-b6aa-4703-9efd-6d8d51dd385f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdSBjheMruK1zpcwcg3aP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P2ypEtQKftGxvxcYZq4orE","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\session-backup-discipline.md","old_string":"- **ASUS backup transfer is UNRESOLVED:** F: can't travel, so the ASUS must back up to its OWN local\n  drive, then move the data to the T480 by network share / USB stick / cloud (method TBD by owner).\n  The self-contained ASUS prompt (inline script, no F: dependency) backs it up locally first.","new_string":"- **ASUS backup transfer RESOLVED via SMB (2026-07-27).** Route = local network share (SMB). What it\n  took on the T480: WiFi profile Public->Private (Public blocks inbound SMB/ICMP), enable File & Printer\n  Sharing (SMB-In + ICMP) for Private, `New-SmbShare -Name backups-inbox -Path F:\\backups`, plus a local\n  `backup` account (MS-account `nsdha` causes SMB auth friction) with share+NTFS write:\n  `Grant-SmbShareAccess -Name backups-inbox -AccountName \"T480\\backup\" -AccessRight Full -Force` and\n  `icacls \"F:\\backups\" /grant \"backup:(OI)(CI)M\"`. ASUS connects with\n  `net use \\\\192.168.68.125\\backups-inbox /user:t480\\backup` (T480 WiFi IP 192.168.68.125). **Passwords\n  are the owner's to type — I never supply/guess/retrieve them** ([[owner-working-style]]); if the\n  `backup` account password is forgotten, owner resets with elevated `net user backup *`. Gate the\n  connect on `(Test-NetConnection 192.168.68.125 -Port 445).TcpTestSucceeded = True`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19748,"cache_read_input_tokens":29306,"output_tokens":918,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19748,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":918,"cache_read_input_tokens":29306,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19748},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"messages_changed","cache_missed_input_tokens":17499}}},"requestId":"req_011CdSBjftC1mvwVvjdghR2X","type":"assistant","uuid":"797d59e2-10b6-4b43-985d-02a4819a3935","timestamp":"2026-07-27T07:42:23.403Z","effort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"468ee845-7d82-4724-a78a-d2a9fbbb431e","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"logical-weaving-pancake"}
{"parentUuid":"797d59e2-10b6-4b43-985d-02a4819a3935","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"176a2f84-f9ed-4295-8be1-772d5178a001","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P2ypEtQKftGxvxcYZq4orE","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\session-backup-discipline.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"927ad2b7-b10f-472e-a4ff-4e7bddcd9d84","timestamp":"2026-07-27T07:42:23.470Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\session-backup-discipline.md","oldString":"- **ASUS backup transfer is UNRESOLVED:** F: can't travel, so the ASUS must back up to its OWN local\n  drive, then move the data to the T480 by network share / USB stick / cloud (method TBD by owner).\n  The self-contained ASUS prompt (inline script, no F: dependency) backs it up locally first.","newString":"- **ASUS backup transfer RESOLVED via SMB (2026-07-27).** Route = local network share (SMB). What it\n  took on the T480: WiFi profile Public->Private (Public blocks inbound SMB/ICMP), enable File & Printer\n  Sharing (SMB-In + ICMP) for Private, `New-SmbShare -Name backups-inbox -Path F:\\backups`, plus a local\n  `backup` account (MS-account `nsdha` causes SMB auth friction) with share+NTFS write:\n  `Grant-SmbShareAccess -Name backups-inbox -AccountName \"T480\\backup\" -AccessRight Full -Force` and\n  `icacls \"F:\\backups\" /grant \"backup:(OI)(CI)M\"`. ASUS connects with\n  `net use \\\\192.168.68.125\\backups-inbox /user:t480\\backup` (T480 WiFi IP 192.168.68.125). **Passwords\n  are the owner's to type — I never supply/guess/retrieve them** ([[owner-working-style]]); if the\n  `backup` account password is forgotten, owner resets with elevated `net user backup *`. Gate the\n  connect on `(Test-NetConnection 192.168.68.125 -Port 445).TcpTestSucceeded = True`.","originalFile":"---\nname: session-backup-discipline\ndescription: \"How AI-session data is backed up across machines — portable F: tool, dated snapshots, fingerprint drift/integrity verification, ASUS prompt\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 468ee845-7d82-4724-a78a-d2a9fbbb431e\n  modified: 2026-07-26T14:44:48.732Z\n---\n\n**Sessions backup system (set up 2026-07-26).** Backs up the AI-session data on each machine to dated,\nverifiable snapshots on two drives, so a LONGVIEW/training cycle can't lose the raw material.\n\n**Drive roles on the T480 (owner-confirmed 2026-07-26): D = live RUNNER, F = static BACKUP.**\n- **D: (internal, ~837 GB free)** is the live runner — all active LONGVIEW/training I/O reads+writes\n  `D:\\benny-home` / `sessions_v1`. Fast internal disk; the pipeline lives here. Run the cycle off D:.\n- **F: (~3.2 TB) is FIXED on the T480 — it CANNOT be disconnected/moved (owner, 2026-07-26).** It is\n  the static verified backup — dated snapshots ONLY, never a live working dir. Separate physical drive\n  from D:, so a D: failure never loses the backup. BUT both D: and F: are inside the one T480 box → this\n  protects against single-drive failure, NOT machine loss/theft/fire. Off-machine protection needs a\n  separate step (cloud sync or a genuinely removable drive) — OPEN.\n- **Cadence:** snapshot D→F before every training run + weekly; `-Mode verify` weekly. Never run the\n  pipeline from F:.\n- **ASUS backup transfer is UNRESOLVED:** F: can't travel, so the ASUS must back up to its OWN local\n  drive, then move the data to the T480 by network share / USB stick / cloud (method TBD by owner).\n  The self-contained ASUS prompt (inline script, no F: dependency) backs it up locally first.\n\n- **Tool (portable):** `F:\\backups\\session-backup.ps1` + `F:\\backups\\README.md` live on the external\n  F: drive (3.2 TB) so they travel between machines. ASCII-only (a `—` em-dash once broke a PS parse).\n  Two modes: `-Mode backup -Dest <root> [-Dest2 <root>] [-Suffix <host>]` and\n  `-Mode verify -Snapshot <path>`.\n- **Sources captured** (a missing one is auto-skipped): `~/.claude` (Claude Code session transcripts),\n  `~/.mem0ray` (memo-ray graph), `D:\\benny-home\\benny\\workspaces\\sessions_v1` (LONGVIEW workspace).\n- **Snapshots:** `<root>\\sessions-<date>[-<host>]\\{claude,mem0ray,sessions_v1}\\` + a `MANIFEST.json`.\n  Copies are robocopy (non-destructive; sources untouched). This machine is the **T480**\n  ([[t480-trainer-stack]]); the other laptop is the **ASUS**.\n- **Drift/integrity = a fingerprint per source** in the manifest: `SHA256(sorted list of\n  relpath|size|mtimeTicks)` + count + bytes + newest-mtime (+ per-file SHA256 for the small ~/.claude\n  set). `-Mode verify` reports per source: INTACT+IN-SYNC (good), INTACT+DRIFT (source moved on →\n  re-run backup), or CORRUPT (snapshot ≠ its manifest → re-run backup to repair). **Remediate =\n  re-run backup** (robocopy idempotent, copies only changed). Run verify weekly + before each\n  LONGVIEW/training run. Same doctrine as the flywheel's L3 durability (replicate→checksum→restore).\n- **Known: `~/.claude` shows DRIFT/verified=false when a Claude session is live** (it is written\n  continuously as I work) — a point-in-time backup of a live dir is expected to differ; mem0ray +\n  sessions_v1 are stable and verify True.\n\n**T480 backup done + verified (2026-07-26):** `D:\\backups\\sessions-2026-07-26` — claude 72→(live-drift),\nmem0ray 80,555 verified, sessions_v1 237,194 verified; total ~317,822 files / 7.6 GB. Mirrored to\n`F:\\backups\\sessions-2026-07-26`.\n\n**ASUS backup (owner runs it there):** connect F: to the ASUS, paste the prompt into a Claude session:\nfind the drive containing `\\backups\\session-backup.ps1`, then\n`session-backup.ps1 -Mode backup -Dest <DRV>backups -Suffix asus`, then `-Mode verify` the snapshot,\nreport the MANIFEST.json totals. It auto-skips the T480-only `D:\\benny-home` source.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines