d_gguf` writes to `<dir>_gguf`**, not the dir you pass.\n26\t5. **Merge peak ~30 GB for a 7B** (fp16 download + merged weights + bf16 GGUF): stage\n27\t   `HF_HOME` and the GGUF output on the SAME roomy drive (D:); a half-C:/half-D: split\n28\t   exhausted C: and crashed the merge with an access violation.\n29\t6. **Store-Python virtualizes %APPDATA%** — config files invisible; pass\n30\t   PRIME_SILO_HOME in env to python subprocesses (t1 gate does this).\n31\t7. **OneDrive repos**: `git config windows.appendAtomically false` or reflog appends fail\n32\t   (`unable to append to .git/logs/HEAD`); index ops are slow; never `git add` a directory\n33\t   that may contain verifier `*.author-bak/` dirs (caused a 250 MB binary commit + history\n34\t   scrub on 2026-07-23).\n35\t8. `node --test <dir>` fails trying to load the dir as a module — point at test files.\n36\t9. **The eGPU wedges transiently** (TB3/RDNA4): a training step just hangs, process alive but\n37\t   blocked, working set collapses to ~MB, no progress for hours. Cap `max_length` lower to\n38\t   reduce memory pressure; verify liveness by CPU-time, never by the tqdm log ([[verify-gpu-job-liveness]]).\n39\t10. DPO (trl 0.23.1 + Unsloth `PatchDPOTrainer()` before `from trl import DPOTrainer`) works on\n40\t    gfx1200: load the SFT adapter as policy, `ref_model=None` (Unsloth uses the adapter-disabled\n41\t    base as reference), `processing_class=tokenizer`, `bf16=True`. DPO doubles memory (chosen+\n42\t    rejected) — keep max_length ≤ 1024.\n43\t\n44\tSee [[t480-trainer-stack]] for the environment itself, [[verify-gpu-job-liveness]] for the\n45\tliveness lesson.\n46\t"}]},"uuid":"a9b5ee87-4c40-4970-a9eb-6c1792241169","timestamp":"2026-07-27T07:45:41.736Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\windows-rocm-training-gotchas.md","content":"---\nname: windows-rocm-training-gotchas\ndescription: Hard-won Windows-ROCm/Un