d rely on a \"Return only JSON\" system prompt (fixed in\n31\t  `benny/core/offload/gate.py::run_judge` for T4).\n32\t- For an ADR-004 **judge**, use a FAST non-reasoning instruct model (gemma-3-4b) — qwen3.5-9b\n33\t  (reasoning) spends its token budget thinking and times out the gate.\n34\t\n35\tModel roster + role mapping (house coder-executor, gemma-3-4b judge, qwen3.5-9b default,\n36\tdeepseek-r1 reasoning, gemma-4-12b-qat LONGVIEW gen, nomic-ai embeddings) is in\n37\t`docs/train/MODEL-ITINERARY.md` — all 8 LLMs + nomic-ai embeddings verified loading+running\n38\ton the eGPU via `lms --gpu max` (2026-07-25); the `cstr` embedding variant fails, use nomic-ai.\n39\t\n40\tSee [[t480-trainer-stack]], [[ep-t-progress]].\n41\t"}]},"uuid":"7798d0b4-bd31-44b3-a3e5-b3942dae3e9c","timestamp":"2026-07-27T07:45:43.248Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\lmstudio-egpu-serving.md","content":"---\nname: lmstudio-egpu-serving\ndescription: How to serve a tuned GGUF via LM Studio on the eGPU + the CLI/API gotchas (T4)\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 61a9f7a2-1353-4f19-addd-895289cb8f19\n  modified: 2026-07-25T11:23:49.605Z\n---\n\nOwner constraint: **serve models only via LM Studio on the eGPU** (not CPU, not standalone\nllama-server, not Ollama), parallelism 1. `lms` CLI at `C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.lmstudio\\bin\\lms.exe`.\n\nServing a custom GGUF:\n- **`lms import` hangs headless** (interactive prompt its `-y` doesn't cover, no stdin).\n  Instead **copy the GGUF directly** into the model tree LM Studio auto-discovers:\n  `C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.lmstudio\\models\\<publisher>\\<repo>-GGUF\\<file>.gguf`.\n- Load key = the GGUF-metadata modelKey from `lms ls --json` (NOT the dir path, NOT\n  publisher/name). E.g. our tuned model's key was bare `qwen2.5-coder-tuned`.\n- `lms load <key> --gpu max --identifier <served-id> -c 4096 -y` — `--identifier` sets the\n  OpenAI model id; `--gpu max` puts it on the eGPU. Suppress the spinner (`>log 2>&1`) — it\n  emits thousands of progress lines.\n- 3 models co-resident fit 16 GB: tuned 7B-q4 (4.7) + gemma-3-4b (3.3) + qwen3.5-9b (6.5) ≈ 14.6.\n\nAPI gotchas (LM Studio OpenAI endpoint :1234/v1):\n- `/v1/models` returns 200 even with **nothing loaded** — check the model id is in the list\n  for a real readiness signal.\n- **Rejects `response_format:{\"type\":\"json_object\"}` with HTTP 400** (`must be 'json_schema'\n  or 'text'`). Lemonade accepts json_object. Provider-agnostic judge/JSON code must retry\n  WITHOUT response_format and rely on a \"Return only JSON\" system prompt (fixed in\n  `benny/core/offload/gate.py::run_judge` for T4).\n- For an ADR-004 **judge**, use a FAST non-reasoning instruct model (gemma-3-4b) — qwen3.5-9b\n  (reasoning) spends its token budget thinking and times out the gate.\n\nModel roster + role mapping (house coder-executor, gemma-3-4b judge, qwen3.5-9b default,\ndeepseek-r1 reasoning, gemma-4-12b-qat LONGVIEW gen, nomic-ai embeddings) is in\n`docs/train/MODEL-ITINERARY.md` — all 8 LLMs + nomic-ai embeddings verified loading+running\non the eGPU via `lms --gpu max` (2026-07-25); the `cstr` embedding variant fails, use nomic-ai.\n\nSee [[t480-trainer-stack]], [[ep-t-progress]].\n","numLines":41,"startLine":1,"totalLines":41}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"91f75c21-30b2-48d2-83f6-72e9b645a0c3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"468ee845-7d82-4724-a78a-d2a9fbbb431e","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"logical-weaving-pancake"}
