{"parentUuid":"213ed6b8-9662-4f81-818d-a15d5f657c55","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"049da3ce-3fb3-453f-9bbd-ee689215ea93","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014bD8WCqcUCrM9bm8qNRTc4","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 2 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Verify against current code before asserting as fact.</system-reminder>\n1\t---\n2\tname: verify-gpu-job-liveness\n3\tdescription: A tqdm/log line is NOT proof a GPU job is alive — verify liveness by CPU-time/artifacts (owner caught a false positive)\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: 61a9f7a2-1353-4f19-addd-895289cb8f19\n8\t  modified: 2026-07-25T05:43:49.032Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t**Never report a long GPU job as \"progressing\" from its log alone.** On 2026-07-25 a DPO run\n12\twedged at step 8/38 (~00:45) and sat frozen for ~6 hours; I read the stale `tqdm` progress\n13\tline and told the owner \"~10 more minutes, training is progressing.\" It was a false positive\n14\tthe owner caught with \"are you sure it's not a false positive.\"\n15\t\n16\t**Why:** `tqdm` writes with `\\r` and, when stderr is redirected to a file, flushes rarely — a\n17\tfrozen log looks identical to a slow one. And the RDNA4 eGPU-over-Thunderbolt **wedges**\n18\ttransiently (a known failure mode for this trainer): the process stays alive but blocked in a\n19\tGPU driver wait, working set collapses to ~1–12 MB (a real 7B training proc holds GBs), and no\n20\tnew steps or checkpoints appear.\n21\t\n22\t**How to apply — prove liveness, don't infer it:**\n23\t- Compare the log's **mtime to now** (`stat -c %y`). Hours stale on a job that should take\n24\t  minutes = wedged, not slow.\n25\t- Confirm the process is **doing work**: take two CPU-time snapshots ~90s apart\n26\t  (`Get-CimInstance Win32_Process ... UserModeTime+KernelModeTime`); a live compute job burns\n27\t  CPU seconds, a wedged one does not. Working-set ~MB = blocked in a syscall.\n28\t- Check for **advancing artifacts** (trainer/checkpoint-*, result JSON, adapter files).\n29\t- To recover: kill the process tree (`Stop-Process -Id <pid> -Force` in PowerShell; use\n30\t  `$procId` not `$id` — `$id:` is a parse error), verify the eGPU recovered with a device\n31\t  matmul, then relaunch (cap `max_length` lower to reduce the memory pressure that can wedge\n32\t  gfx1200). Background-poll CPU-time to confirm the relaunch is genuinely stepping.\n33\t\n34\tSee [[windows-rocm-training-gotchas]], [[t480-trainer-stack]].\n35\t"}]},"uuid":"46c0b87e-1e84-4353-8208-28b982b4bd83","timestamp":"2026-07-27T07:45:43.548Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\verify-gpu-job-liveness.md","content":"---\nname: verify-gpu-job-liveness\ndescription: A tqdm/log line is NOT proof a GPU job is alive — verify liveness by CPU-time/artifacts (owner caught a false positive)\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 61a9f7a2-1353-4f19-addd-895289cb8f19\n  modified: 2026-07-25T05:43:49.032Z\n---\n\n**Never report a long GPU job as \"progressing\" from its log alone.** On 2026-07-25 a DPO run\nwedged at step 8/38 (~00:45) and sat frozen for ~6 hours; I read the stale `tqdm` progress\nline and told the owner \"~10 more minutes, training is progressing.\" It was a false positive\nthe owner caught with \"are you sure it's not a false positive.\"\n\n**Why:** `tqdm` writes with `\\r` and, when stderr is redirected to a file, flushes rarely — a\nfrozen log looks identical to a slow one. And the RDNA4 eGPU-over-Thunderbolt **wedges**\ntransiently (a known failure mode for this trainer): the process stays alive but blocked in a\nGPU driver wait, working set collapses to ~1–12 MB (a real 7B training proc holds GBs), and no\nnew steps or checkpoints appear.\n\n**How to apply — prove liveness, don't infer it:**\n- Compare the log's **mtime to now** (`stat -c %y`). Hours stale on a job that should take\n  minutes = wedged, not slow.\n- Confirm the process is **doing work**: take two CPU-time snapshots ~90s apart\n  (`Get-CimInstance Win32_Process ... UserModeTime+KernelModeTime`); a live compute job burns\n  CPU seconds, a wedged one does not. Working-set ~MB = blocked in a syscall.\n- Check for **advancing artifacts** (trainer/checkpoint-*, result JSON, adapter files).\n- To recover: kill the process tree (`Stop-Process -Id <pid> -Force` in PowerShell; use\n  `$procId` not `$id` — `$id:` is a parse error), verify the eGPU recovered with a device\n  matmul, then relaunch (cap `max_length` lower to reduce the memory pressure that can wedge\n  gfx1200). Background-poll CPU-time to confirm the relaunch is genuinely stepping.\n\nSee [[windows-rocm-training-gotchas]], [[t480-trainer-stack]].\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"213ed6b8-9662-4f81-818d-a15d5f657c55","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"468ee845-7d82-4724-a78a-d2a9fbbb431e","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"logical-weaving-pancake"}
