{"parentUuid":"58ca42fa-e924-43bf-9eb3-aa137746c3ae","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"049da3ce-3fb3-453f-9bbd-ee689215ea93","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UtrrPaknMX6sJnUet1do9n","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: longview-pipeline\n3\tdescription: Operate, analyze, or extend the LONGVIEW session-synthesis pipeline (cards, graph, reports, book, audiobook). Use when working on scripts/longview, reviewing card output, planning card schema changes, or debugging a LONGVIEW run.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# LONGVIEW pipeline — operational knowledge\n7\t\n8\tLONGVIEW map-reduces months of agent sessions (memo-ray store) into per-session **cards** via a local\n9\tmodel, then graph + themes + report/book/PDF/audiobook.\n10\tPipeline: inventory → extract → map(walk) → (model **or** graph) → code → weave → enrich → review → reduce(TIMELINE) → opus → pdf.\n11\tCode: `scripts/longview/`. Guide: `runtime/docs/operations/LONGVIEW_GUIDE.md`.\n12\t\n13\t**Governance & observability (v1.16.x) — all deterministic, ledger-sourced:**\n14\t- **Memory teleport** (`memory.mjs` + `memory_graph.py`): label→resolve→teleport sensitive sessions (CV/job) to a quarantine workspace (moves files + Neo4j nodes + Chroma chunks, journalled, reversible via `restore`); `quarantine.json` filters teleported sids from inventory forever; `lib/leak_gate.mjs` gates deliverables. Graph Source names use the **8-char sid prefix**, not the 32-char card filename. UI: `:8788/memory.html`.\n15\t- **Dashboard** (`scratch/longview_run/dashboard/`, `bash dash.sh` → `:8788`): Mission Control (`/`) + Lineage/governance (`/lineage.html`, OpenLineage DAG + artifact explorer + step-through reusing `lib/record.mjs` + execution register) + `/kindle.html` (ES5). Every number derives from `ledger.jsonl` + disk — no hidden state.\n16\t- **Arc-driven opus** (`lib/arcs.mjs`): timeline-walked cross-project arcs feed sections; `draft → gate → critique → revise`. `LONGVIEW_OPUS_DIR=iterations/<name>` builds without clobbering a prior book.\n17\t- **Coverage gotcha:** `.meta.json` also ends in `.json` — always `filter(f=>f.endsWith('.json') && !f.endsWith('.meta.json'))` or card counts / coverage denominators double.\n18\t- **Ingest wedge fix:** server-side `deep_synthesis` ingest kept flooding the LM host after client death — `POST /api/rag/ingest/cancel` + `GET /api/rag/ingest/active` + a 3-strike connectivity circuit breaker. `subprocessEnv()` forwards repo `.env` to spawned python (else LM endpoints unseen). `reasoning_effort:\"none\"` + empty-content→`reasoning_content` fallback (post-restart LM Studio diverts the whole reply into reasoning).\n19\t\n20\t**Model is env/profile-driven** (not hardcoded): `BENNY_DEFAULT_MODEL` / `LONGVIEW_MODEL` pick it,\n21\tthe manifest carries only a preconfigured default. Verified LAN setup: LM Studio on\n22\t`192.168.68.125:1234` serving `lmstudio/google/gemma-4-12b` (a reasoning model — the per-call token\n23\tbudget must clear its ~500-1000-tok preamble, e.g. `LONGVIEW_FRAGMENT_MAX_TOKENS=1800`, or content\n24\tcomes back empty → blank cards; full org/model id required; `response_format` must be `json_schema|text`,\n25\tnever `json_object`). A wedged gemma engine returns HTTP 200 but zero tokens — reload the model on the\n26\tLM host to reset it; embeddings on the same host still answering isolates it as generation-specific.\n27\t\n28\t**Graph build — two paths, same schema (Source/Concept/RELATES_TO/SOURCED_FROM):**\n29\t- `model` = deep_synthesis: a second LLM pass re-extracts triples per card section. ~60-120s/card.\n30\t- `graph` = **longview_v2, deterministic**: builds triples directly from the card's own\n31\t  `concepts[]`/`applications[]`/`capabilities[]`/`skills_observed[]` — no model call, **~0.4s/card**.\n32\t  `(:Project)-[INVOLVES/USES/DEMONSTRATES/APPLIES]->` entities + an anchor `CO_OCCURS_WITH` star per card.\n33\t  The map phase already distilled the entities once, so re-extraction is redundant — `graph` is the\n34\t  speed lever. Then run `enrich` to merge duplicate concepts across cards into shared hubs.\n35\t  Code: `lib/card_triples.mjs` (pure `buildCardTriples`), server route `POST /rag/graph-upsert`\n36\t  (→ `save_knowledge_triples`, no clustering), live earned-ETA via `lib/eta.mjs` → `<ws>/longview/progress.json`.\n37\t  Sentence-shaped fields (decisions/outcomes/failures) are deliberately NOT nodes — they stay in the card\n38\t  md for vectors. Blank cards (no entities) are counted + skipped, never written as empty hubs.\n39\t\n40\t## Hard-won constraints (violate these and the run fails slowly)\n41\t\n42\t- **ONE clean call at a time — never probe the LM host during a run (2026-07-09).** A second\n43\t  concurrent request, or an aborted in-flight call, wedges the LM Studio engine →\n44\t  `{\"_error\":\"Engine protocol predict request failed: fetch failed\"}` (400) on every subsequent\n45\t  predict, while `/v1/models` still says `loaded` and embeddings still answer. Recovery = eject +\n46\t  reload the model on the LM host (no HTTP unload). Do diagnostic/health probes ONLY between runs\n47\t  with the runner stopped. Any timing measured while a probe competed with the map is inflated —\n48\t  discard it. This bit us live: the \"gemma is slow / 56s probe / 1835s card\" numbers were all self-\n49\t  inflicted concurrency, and killing a queued probe is what wedged the engine.\n50\t- **Turn off reasoning on extraction calls (2026-07-09) — the 4× lever.** gemma-4-12b burns ~78% of\n51\t  every call on a reasoning preamble that adds nothing to a *reading* task (verified: 640→0 reasoning\n52\t  tokens, JSON still full/valid, 16-window card 160s/win → 42s/win). The prompt CANNOT suppress it and\n53\t  `enable_thinking:false` / `thinking:false` / `reasoning_effort:\"low\"` are ignored — the working\n54\t  control is the request param **`reasoning_effort:\"none\"`** (LM Studio honors it; it's on/off, not\n55\t  low/med/high). Wired as `LONGVIEW_REASONING_EFFORT` → `llm.mjs`; env-gated so it's omitted for\n56\t  providers that would reject it. Quality held completely (all 13 fields, rich concepts).\n57\t- **LM-host hardware = AMD RDNA4 eGPU (2026-07-09) — the wedge is a driver/runtime problem, not config.**\n58\t  The LAN LM Studio (`192.168.68.125:1234`) runs an **AMD RX 9060 XT 16 GB (RDNA4)** in a **Razer Core X\n59\t  eGPU over Thunderbolt** on a T480. The recurring `channel error` / `Engine protocol predict request\n60\t  failed` wedge (~every 1 session under sustained load) is **RDNA4/ROCm + eGPU instability, NOT VRAM**\n61\t  (16 GB fits a 12B) and NOT a longview setting — window-size, context, and reasoning tuning did NOT fix\n62\t  it (all tried). Levers: LM Studio **ROCm concurrency=1** + **disable experimental KV-cache share** +\n63\t  map cooldown `LONGVIEW_WINDOW_PAUSE_MS` (~2000ms between window calls). **Vulkan is the stable AMD\n64\t  runtime but won't load a 12B** (large-model Vulkan limit) → durable fix if ROCm keeps crashing is a\n65\t  **7–8B instruct model (Qwen2.5-7B / Llama-3.1-8B) on Vulkan** (the map is extraction — a 7–8B suffices;\n66\t  verify 2–3 cards). Don't blind-reload on repeat; check runtime + consider the smaller-model path.\n67\t- **Halt on an engine wedge, don't march through it (2026-07-09).** LM Studio's engine wedges\n68\t  spontaneously under sustained load → `Engine protocol predict request failed: fetch failed` (400) on\n69\t  every predict until reloaded. This is INDEPENDENT of reasoning on/off (seen both ways). The map now\n70\t  detects the wedge (`isEngineWedge`), does NOT cache the failed window (so resume retries it), stops\n71\t  the phase, and exits non-zero so build_v2.sh halts before graph/enrich. Recovery: reload the model on\n72\t  the host, rerun — resume re-maps the unwritten sessions. Root-cause needs LM Studio's OWN logs\n73\t  (OOM/KV-cache → lower ctx or GPU layers; GPU error → host; poison input → re-crashes same session).\n74\t- **Window size vs timeout on a reasoning model (2026-07-09).** Full 24k-char windows on gemma-4-12b\n75\t  overran the 200s `LONGVIEW_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS` (prefill ~6.9k tok + ~1000-tok reasoning preamble + output)\n76\t  and got amputated → `{\"_error\":\"...aborted due to timeout\"}`, ~31% window loss on multi-window cards.\n77\t  Fix that held: `LONGVIEW_WINDOW_CHARS=12000` + `LONGVIEW_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=420000` → 0 timeouts.\n78\t  Tradeoff: smaller windows = more calls/session, and gemma's reasoning tax is paid **per call**\n79\t  (~90% of a small call's tokens are reasoning), so single-window sessions get ~2× slower. Distinguish\n80\t  the two error strings: \"aborted due to timeout\" = shrink window / raise timeout; \"Engine protocol\n81\t  predict request failed\" = engine wedge, reload the model. Purge affected cards+window dirs to re-map.\n82\t- **Backlog then top-up.** Map the whole corpus once (all sessions), then `longview run --delta` for\n83\t  incremental top-ups — don't cut scope to go faster; fix throughput instead.\n84\t- **Local model output is short.** ~415-token self-truncation observed; 500 proven max (live telemetry\n85\t  2026-07-05). Window every extraction (`lib/walk.mjs`), assemble cards **losslessly in code** — never ask\n86\t  the model for a whole card.\n87\t- **Prefill dominates cost:** TTFT 22 s @ 7.7k input, 8.33 tok/s. Prefer few, full windows over many small\n88\t  calls. Estimate `calls × (TTFT + out/TPS)` before launching a run.\n89\t- **16k ctx** via `~/.cache/lemonade/recipe_options.json` per-model `ctx_size` + restart with\n90\t  `POST /api/v1/load` (never a chat call right after killing flm.exe — it races the respawn).\n91\t- **Workspace precedence:** a manifest's hardcoded `workspace` silently overrode env once (killed a run).\n92\t  Always verify the `[run] … → workspace 'X'` log line after launch.\n93\t- **Never disturb a live run** — analysis of cards/ledger is read-only; normalizations run post-hoc.\n94\t- **One run = one model/engine (A8, fixed v1.1