{"parentUuid":"49c79e5f-48ef-45fa-8f48-c92964b1ae58","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"049da3ce-3fb3-453f-9bbd-ee689215ea93","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JRFUcV1UEkikR5e8tEUKfp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: prime-silo-experience\n3\tdescription: The Prime-Silo product experience contract — identity (Prime-Silo + Agent Benny, never Space Agent), earth-tone design tokens, progressive-discovery doctrine, and the \"motion is meaning\" choreography rules that bring animejs.com-grade kinetics INTO the app without violating the C0 calm contract. Use for any user-facing UI work in app/, server/pages/, or packaging/ (login, first-run, shell, mascot, Studio, Bridge).\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# The Prime-Silo experience — identity, discovery, motion\n7\t\n8\tThe product is **Prime-Silo**. The guide who lives inside it is **Agent Benny** (the german\n9\tshepherd). \"Space Agent\" is a dead upstream name — it must never appear on a user-facing surface\n10\t(strings, titles, alt text, logos, docs prose). Identifiers (`space-desktop:` IPC, `node space`\n11\tCLI, file names, package names) are protected until Workstream H — do not rename them.\n12\t\n13\tThe feeling to build: **walking into a quiet, beautifully organized grain silo with a very good\n14\tdog showing you around.** Calm by default; kinetic at the exact moments that deserve it. The\n15\tmarketing site (website/) already nails this — the app must feel like the same product.\n16\t\n17\t## 1. One palette, two surfaces\n18\t\n19\tAll app color resolves through `var(--*)` tokens in\n20\t`app/L0/_all/mod/_core/framework/css/colors.css` (enforced by `scripts/gates/c0.mjs` — hex\n21\tliterals outside colors.css fail the commit). The family: alabaster/cream grounds, moss/charcoal\n22\tgreens for depth, rust for the ONE primary action, sage/taupe for structure. Depth = the three\n23\t`--elevation-1/2/3` tokens only. Spacing/radius/measure from `layout.css`, type from `type.css`\n24\t(base ≥16px, line-height 1.5, ≤70ch, never justify). Read `architecture/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` in\n25\tfull before any CSS — it is short and it is law.\n26\t\n27\t## 2. Progressive discovery (the ADHD contract, C0)\n28\t\n29\t- **One decision per screen.** First-run, wizards, and setup flows present exactly one choice,\n30\t  then advance. Never a settings wall.\n31\t- **One primary action per view**, rust-accented, visually dominant. Everything secondary sits\n32\t  behind a consistent `More ▸` disclosure.\n33\t- **Teach by doing.** Empty states offer the first action, not documentation (\"Drop a PDF to\n34\t  begin\"). After the first success, suggest exactly 3 next actions.\n35\t- **Long work is honest work:** always `Step n of m` + one plain line of \"what happens next.\"\n36\t  Progress lands as a card, never a modal wait.\n37\t- Benny narrates transitions in first person, short and warm: \"I'll keep your documents on this\n38\t  machine.\" — never marketing voice inside the product.\n39\t\n40\t## 3. Motion doctrine — \"motion is meaning\"\n41\t\n42\tC0 says: *no ambient motion; animation only as feedback to user action* (mascot micro-states are\n43\tthe sanctioned exception). This is NOT a ban on the animejs.com aesthetic — it is a targeting\n44\trule. The website proves the style; the app earns it at these moments:\n45\t\n46\t**Sanctioned kinetic moments (choreograph these fully):**\n47\t1. **Threshold moments** — login load, first-run steps, section transitions the USER initiated.\n48\t   A step change is user action; a spring-staggered entrance of the next step IS feedback.\n49\t2. **State becoming visible** — a run starting (DAG nodes light in sequence), ingestion\n50\t   progressing (dial arc sweeps to the real fraction), a graph materializing (nodes settle with\n51\t   springs, edges draw with `createDrawable`). The animation must be DRIVEN BY REAL EVENTS\n52\t   (SSE/EventBus), never a timer pretending. If the data didn't move, the pixels don't move.\n53\t3. **Benny micro-states** — idle (breathing ear/tail, subtle), listening (head tilt on input\n54\t   focus), processing (bound to real SSE activity). The only allowed loop, and it must be quiet.\n55\t\n56\t**Forbidden:** looping decorative backgrounds, parallax for its own sake, attention-grabbing\n57\tpulses on idle UI, anything that moves while the user is reading and nothing is happening.\n58\t\n59\t**Hard gates on every animation, no exceptions:**\n60\t```js\n61\tconst calm = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches\n62\t  || document.documentElement.dataset.profile === 'zen';   // C7 Zen = zero animation\n63\tif (calm) return;  // final state must already be in the CSS — page complete with zero JS\n64\t```\n65\t\n66\t**Vocabulary (same as the website — one motion language):** springs with slight overshoot\n67\t(`createSpring({stiffness:120, damping:12})`), `out(3..5)` eases, 500–900ms, `stagger(40–80)` on\n68\tanything plural, SVG stroke-draw for diagrams, counters that count to REAL numbers. Use the\n69\tvendored anime.js v4 ESM — vendor it for the app at\n70\t`app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/vendor/anime.esm.min.js` (copy from `website/vendor/`). The verified\n71\tv4 API + idioms + mobile rules live in `.claude/skills/animejs-scrollcraft/SKILL.md` — read it\n72\tbefore writing a single `animate()` call; API drift is the #1 historical failure source.\n73\t\n74\t## 4. Set-piece patterns (reuse, don't reinvent)\n75\t\n76\t- **The Silo** (identity moment): stroke-drawn silo assembling from ring segments — login and\n77\t  brand thresholds. Reference implementation: `website/build.mjs` (heroSiloSvg/siloChapterSvg).\n78\t- **The Dial** (any pipeline): N nodes on a ring, sweeping progress arc, active node blooms,\n79\t  center readout swaps per step. Reference: `website/` dial chapter. In-app version binds the\n80\t  arc to real progress (G0 run events / progress.json fractions), not scroll.\n81\t- **Terminal cinema** (honest logs): moss-dark Courier block, typed lines, count-up numbers —\n82\t  for run output surfaces. Never fake the log content.\n83\t- **Benny walk** (guidance): Benny moves along a path between steps of a flow, sits at the\n84\t  active one. Source art: `app/L0/_all/mod/_core/visual/res/chat/overlay/dog_no_bg.svg`\n85\t  (body parts are commented per-path — split into <symbol> parts for posing, as website did).\n86\t\n87\t## 5. First-impression flows (the taste bar)\n88\t\n89\t**Login** = \"enter the silo\": alabaster ground, the silo drawing itself once (~1.2s, then still),\n90\tBenny sitting beside the form, rust primary button, moss focus rings. No gradients from space,\n91\tno starfields. **First-run** = four screens, one decision each (welcome → home dir → services\n92\tcheck → done); Benny walks the rail between steps; the services check animates real probe\n93\tresults as they return. Every flow must be fully usable — and look intentional, final states\n94\tin CSS — with JS disabled or reduced-motion on.\n95\t\n96\t## 6. Verification (what \"done\" looks like)\n97\t\n98\t1. `node scripts/gates/c0.mjs` green after ANY CSS touch.\n99\t2. Preview at 1280×800 AND 375×812 (the app gets narrow windows too — panes, not pages).\n100\t3. `prefers-reduced-motion` emulation: zero running animations, page fully readable.\n101\t4. Zen profile (when C7 lands): same as reduced motion.\n102\t5. Screenshot the moment of delight AND the calm resting state — both must pass taste review:\n103\t   would this feel at home next to https://binary16labs.github.io/prime-silo/ ?\n104\t6. Grep your diff for `Space Agent|space agent` — zero user-facing hits.\n105\t"}]},"uuid":"792acaf3-24ef-4168-8cc2-8ab452066a5c","timestamp":"2026-07-27T08:37:24.875Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\.claude\\skills\\prime-silo-experience\\SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: prime-silo-experience\ndescription: The Prime-Silo product experience contract — identity (P