{"parentUuid":"23dfe1df-d76f-4246-9849-493ac636859b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"049da3ce-3fb3-453f-9bbd-ee689215ea93","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RJvPNZ6DsMRmUmojoPq7jn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: delivery-board\n3\tdescription: Operate the Prime-Silo delivery board (delivery/) autonomously — select, claim, execute, verify, and log work contracts without frontier supervision. Use whenever picking up a task from delivery/board/BOARD.md, authoring a gate script, verifying another agent's task, or deciding which model tier should take which contract.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# Delivery-board operator — run the board without supervision\n7\t\n8\tThe board at `delivery/board/BOARD.md` is the single source of work. `delivery/README.md` is the\n9\tlaw — read it once per session, follow it exactly. This skill adds what README assumes you know:\n10\tthe mechanics, the tier routing, and the traps that have actually burned agents in this repo.\n11\t\n12\t## 1. The loop (memorize this shape)\n13\t\n14\t```\n15\tread README → read BOARD → take TOPMOST READY item → claim (board edit + LOG line + commit)\n16\t→ read ONLY your contract (delivery/tasks/<ID>.md) → make a worktree if sandbox: worktree\n17\t→ TDD: failing test/gate FIRST, watch it fail → implement inside the allowlist → gate green\n18\t→ move board line to VERIFY + LOG `ready-for-verify` + commit → STOP (never self-DONE)\n19\t```\n20\t\n21\t- **Claim commit message:** `chore(delivery): claim <ID>` · **work commits:** `feat(<ID>): <what>` /\n22\t  `test(<ID>): <scenario name>` · **verify handoff:** `chore(delivery): <ID> ready-for-verify`.\n23\t- **LOG format (append-only, never edit):** `<ISO-ts> | <ID> | <event> | <agent> | <note>`\n24\t  Events: `claimed`, `ready-for-verify`, `verified-by`, `blocked`, `unblocked`, `note`.\n25\t- **Agent identity:** use `<harness>-<tier>` (e.g. `claude-sonnet`, `claude-haiku-verifier`).\n26\t- **Promotion rule:** when the last dep of an AUTHORED item is verified DONE, move it to the\n27\t  BOTTOM of READY with a note `(dep <X> DONE — entered READY <date>)`. Anyone may promote;\n28\t  only the human reorders READY.\n29\t- **Two strikes → blocked.** Same failure twice: log `blocked` with the exact error and what you\n30\t  tried. Do not redesign around the contract. Do not brute-force a third attempt.\n31\t\n32\t## 2. Model-tier routing (who takes what)\n33\t\n34\t| Tier | Takes | Never takes |\n35\t|---|---|---|\n36\t| **haiku** | Independent VERIFICATION of others' tasks (re-run gate from clean checkout, tick BDD scenarios, move VERIFY→DONE), mechanical single-surface contracts (grep-and-replace passes like C4 execution, LOG/board hygiene, running gates) | Contract authoring, anything with design judgment, multi-file architecture, writing new gates |\n37\t| **sonnet** | Standard contracts: layout/CSS work (C1), SSE/API endpoints (B1), keyframe+binding work (C5), test suites, gate scripts from a spec, docs passes | Contract authoring/splitting, taste-defining UI (first impressions), cross-workstream tradeoffs |\n38\t| **opus** | Design-taste flagships (C3 login/first-run, D1 Studio spec, E-workstream visual), contract authoring/splitting at plan checkpoints, anything touching >2 workstreams, unblocking a task two tiers failed | Bulk mechanical work (wasteful) |\n39\t\n40\tVerification is ALWAYS a different identity than the author — a fresh session/agent with no shared\n41\tcontext, reading only the contract + README, from a clean checkout. Haiku is the default verifier;\n42\tescalate to sonnet if the gate involves preview/screenshot judgment.\n43\t\n44\t## 3. Worktree recipe (sandbox: worktree)\n45\t\n46\tThe repo lives under OneDrive; put worktrees OUTSIDE it so sync doesn't thrash:\n47\t\n48\t```bash\n49\tgit -C /c/Users/nsdha/OneDrive/binary16/prime-silo worktree add \\\n50\t  /c/Users/nsdha/.ps-worktrees/<ID> -b task/<ID> main\n51\t```\n52\t\n53\tWork + commit there. When the gate is green, hand off; the merger (or verifier) does\n54\t`git merge --no-ff task/<ID>` on main after verification, then\n55\t`git worktree remove /c/Users/nsdha/.ps-worktrees/<ID>`.\n56\tBoard/LOG edits are made on MAIN directly (they are coordination, not task payload) —\n57\tclaim before creating the worktree so the claim is visible to everyone immediately.\n58\tIf `node_modules` are needed in the worktree: `npm ci --prefix server` (only if your gate\n59\tactually requires the server; static-analysis gates should stay zero-dep).\n60\t\n61\t## 4. Gate-script craft (scripts/gates/*.mjs)\n62\t\n63\tStudy `scripts/gates/c0.mjs` and `w0.mjs` before writing one. House style:\n64\t- Zero-dep Node ESM (`node:fs`, `node:path`, `node:child_process` only). Exit 0 = pass,\n65\t  non-zero = fail **naming the file and the rule violated** (a gate that fails silently is a defect).\n66\t- Prefer static analysis (grep/parse the source) over spinning up servers. If a preview is\n67\t  unavoidable (C1 screenshots), make the gate degrade honestly: check what it can statically,\n68\t  print `MANUAL: <what the verifier must eyeball>` for the rest.\n69\t- Ratchet pattern for pre-existing violations: record the floor inline (`VIOLATION_FLOOR`),\n70\t  fail only if the count RISES or a new file offends (see c0.mjs).\n71\t- A gate must fail-as-designed first: run it against the pre-change tree and watch it exit\n72\t  non-zero before you implement. That IS the TDD red step for infra tasks.\n73\t\n74\t## 5. Traps that have actually burned agents here\n75\t\n76\t1. **`.env` contains `BENNY_HMAC_KEY` — never staged, never committed.** Same for `logs/`,\n77\t   `brain/`, `scratch/`, `site/` (unrelated WIP), and any live run workspace. Stage files BY NAME,\n78\t   never `git add -A`.\n79\t2. **The tree usually has unrelated uncommitted changes** (owner's WIP). Do not touch, stash,\n80\t   or commit them. Worktrees sidestep this — another reason to use them.\n81\t3. **Allowlist is literal.** Needing one file outside it = `blocked`, not improvisation. Tests\n82\t   for your scenarios are implied-allowed (put them in `tests/` or next to the gate).\n83\t4. **Budget = changed lines excluding tests/lockfiles.** Over budget → log `blocked: needs split`.\n84\t5. **Governed CSS is linted by c0.mjs on every commit** — no hex outside `colors.css`, no\n85\t   `text-align: justify`, base font ≥16px, exactly 3 elevation tokens. Read\n86\t   `architecture/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` before touching any CSS. Your task's gate should CALL c0\n87\t   if you touched governed CSS.\n88\t6. **Windows + Git Bash:** shell scripts run under Git Bash (`/c/Users/...` paths); Node is the\n89\t   portable choice for gates. PowerShell 5.1 has no `&&`.\n90\t7. **Do not call the LAN LM host** (192.168.68.125:1234) — a LONGVIEW run may be in flight and\n91\t   concurrent probes wedge the engine. UI/board tasks never need it.\n92\t8. **Old routes keep working** — every UI change ships behind a flag or is additive\n93\t   (protocol rule: `PRIME_SILO_NEW_SHELL` pattern). Breaking the default experience = blocked.\n94\t9. **UI tasks read `.claude/skills/prime-silo-experience/SKILL.md`** (identity, motion doctrine,\n95\t   progressive discovery) and, if animating, `.claude/skills/animejs-scrollcraft/SKILL.md`\n96\t   (the verified anime.js v4 API — API drift is the #1 historical failure source).\n97\t\n98\t## 6. Repo map for board work (verified paths)\n99\t\n100\t- Board/law: `delivery/board/BOARD.md`, `delivery/board/LOG.md`, `delivery/README.md`\n101\t- Contracts: `delivery/tasks/<ID>.md` · template: `delivery/tasks/_TEMPLATE.md`\n102\t- Plan narrative: `architecture/PLAN-local-power-unified-ui.md` (§ per workstream)\n103\t- Design law: `architecture/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` + `app/L0/_all/mod/_core/framework/css/{colors,layout,type}.css`\n104\t- Gates: `scripts/gates/` · Login page: `server/pages/login.html` (+ enter.html, index.html)\n105\t- Mascot/onscreen agent: `app/L0/_all/mod/_core/onscreen_agent/panel.html`\n106\t- Prime-Silo modules: `app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/` · widgets: `app/L0/_all/mod/_core/widgets/`\n107\t- UI-UX findings: `architecture/REQUIREMENTS-ui-ux-refactor.md` (C3/C5 source — don't re-audit)\n108\t- Launch configs for preview: `../.claude/launch.json` (binary16 root; `shell` = the app on :3000)\n109\t\n110\t## 7. Definition of done (verifier checklist)\n111\t\n112\tAll BDD scenarios have named tests · `verify` exits 0 from a clean checkout · lint/format clean ·\n113\tallowlist respected (diff audit) · budget respected · board+LOG updated at every transition ·\n114\tdocs/skills updated if the contract's Handoff says so · author ≠ verifier.\n115\t"}]},"uuid":"ab3f31f4-a8ef-4f5a-bff0-336968b9e669","timestamp":"2026-07-27T08:45:23.716Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\.claude\\skills\\delivery-board\\SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: delivery-board\ndescription: Operate the Prime-Silo delivery board (delivery/) autonomously — select, claim, execute, verify, and log work contracts without frontier supervision. Use whenever picking up a task from delivery/board/BOARD.md, authoring a gate script, verifying another agent's task, or deciding which model tier should take which contract.\n---\n\n# Delivery-board operator — run the board without supervision\n\nThe board at `delivery/board/BOARD.md` is the single source of work. `delivery/README.md` is the\nlaw — read it once per session, follow it exactly. This skill adds what README assumes you know:\nthe mechanics, the tier routing, and the traps that have actually burned agents in this repo.\n\n## 1. The loop (memorize this shape)\n\n```\nread README → read BOARD → take TOPMOST READY item → claim (board edit + LOG line + commit)\n→ read ONLY your contract (delivery/tasks/<ID>.md) → make a worktree if sandbox: worktree\n→ TDD: failing test/gate FIRST, watch it fail → implement inside the allowlist → gate green\n→ move board line to VERI